# The browser build has no server, so Vercel has no reason to install Python.
#
# Without this, the presence of requirements.txt makes Vercel treat the repo as a
# Python project and it then fails the build demanding a WSGI/ASGI entrypoint
# (app.py / index.py / server.py / main.py / wsgi.py / asgi.py).
#
# requirements.txt is still committed and is what `pip install -r requirements.txt`
# uses locally and what Streamlit Community Cloud reads. It is only hidden from
# the Vercel build.
requirements.txt
